A||||0||theogre||87-88 4 cyl VSS feed to ECM. ECM Interchange||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||07-14-2001||03:35 PM||||As I've mentioned in other threads,Grand AM and Olds Cutlass Caliase use the same ECM as 87-88 Fiero 4 cyl. The only diferance is the PROM in them.<P>In those cars the ECM's PROM is programmed to select direct feed VSS instead of Fiero's dash buffered VSS.<P>Someone here already has one of those PROMs already. You need to do this patch to stop the code 24.<P>The ECM will set code 24 and Cruise control will not operate unless the VSS is patched to the ECM.<P>To use direct VSS PROMs in Fiero:<P>Patch ECM connector Black Terminal 6 to connector C203 terminal G (The terminal markings are molded into the connector shells.)<P>C203 is the large connector sitting below the ECM. Terminal G contains a Yellow wire between a Green and Pink/Black wire.<P>Terminals for the ECM connectors are MotorMite # 85323<P>You can splice the yellow wire described above with any method you like. Just make absolutly sure it can't come loose or short.<P><BR>The ECM is located under the passenger side of the dash on both Grand Am and Olds Cutlass Calaise. If you are harvesting the ECM, cut out the connectors with as much wire as you can get. This will give you a bunch of prewired spare terminals.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
